On a Nokia 7750 SR, when BGP is choosing between multiple paths from the same neighbor AS, how do I force it to consistently prioritize the route with the lowest "metric value" advertised by that AS, even if some routes are advertised later? I’ve seen cases where the order in which updates arrive affects which path gets picked, even though the metrics are static—how do I lock this down so it’s always metric-based?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure BGP consistently prioritizes the route with the lowest MED value from the same neighbor AS, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    deterministic-med
exit
```

This forces BGP to group paths by neighbor AS before comparing MED values, eliminating path selection dependencies on update arrival order. The selection will now always prefer the lowest MED within each neighbor AS group.
