To lock down your BGP session to strictly IPv4-only exchanges and prevent any capability negotiation, apply the following configuration at the neighbor level:

```console
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <neighbor-IP>
                disable-capability-negotiation
```

**Important notes:**
1. Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-IP>` with your specific BGP group name and neighbor IP address.
2. After applying this configuration, you **must reset the BGP session** (e.g., `clear router bgp peer <neighbor-IP>`) for the change to take effect.
3. This command will force the session to:
   - Operate in legacy IPv4-only mode
   - Ignore all modern BGP capabilities (MP-BGP, 4-byte ASN, etc.)
   - Disable any capability negotiation during session establishment

The session will now only exchange basic IPv4 routes without attempting any extended feature negotiation.
