To ensure your Nokia 7750 SR properly advertises BGP graceful restart capability for NOTIFICATION messages when the remote peer supports it, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
    exit
```

This enables the router to:
1. Advertise its ability to handle "we’re going down" NOTIFICATION messages in BGP graceful restart capabilities.
2. Only activate this behavior when the remote peer also signals support for the feature.
3. Preserve traffic during session restarts when both peers negotiate this capability.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
If I'm working with a Nokia 7750 SR and want its BGP neighbor session restarts to not drop traffic, how do I tweak the settings so it explicitly tells peers it can handle those "we’re going down" messages properly—but only when the remote side also says it can play nice with that feature? Currently, even when both sides agree, the router isn’t advertising this handshake correctly.
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure your Nokia 7750 SR properly advertises BGP graceful restart capability for NOTIFICATION messages when the remote peer supports it, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
    exit
```

This enables the router to:
1. Advertise its ability to handle "we’re going down" NOTIFICATION messages in BGP graceful restart capabilities.
2. Only activate this behavior when the remote peer also signals support for the feature.
3. Preserve traffic during session restarts when both peers negotiate this capability.
