To address the issue of lingering BGP paths not being advertised after a restart, apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors without-no-export
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
- **`long-lived`**: Enables BGP Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) to manage stale routes.
- **`advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors without-no-export`**: Forces the router to advertise stale routes to **all neighbors** (including those without LLGR capability) and removes the `no-export` community. This ensures stale routes propagate beyond the local AS.

This configuration ensures leftover routes are actively advertised to all neighbors and exit your network domain. Adjust the `stale-routes-time` under `graceful-restart` if you need to extend how long stale routes are retained (e.g., `stale-routes-time 600`).
