To achieve BGP path selection based on the lowest total internal IGP cost, use the AIGP attribute to incorporate end-to-end IGP metrics into BGP decisions. Enable AIGP support on relevant BGP groups or neighbors:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "your_group_name"
        aigp
    exit
exit
```

**Key notes:**
1. AIGP must be consistently enabled on all participating BGP peers to propagate and accumulate IGP metrics
2. Routes will be compared using the cumulative IGP metric after standard attributes like Local Preference
3. Ensure IGP metrics are properly configured and consistent across the network

For granular control, apply AIGP to specific neighbors:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "your_group_name"
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            aigp
        exit
    exit
exit
```
