To achieve your goal of using only custom static paths (excluding the default route) for resolving BGP-labeled IPv4 traffic next-hops, use these CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            allow-static
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution filter
                    resolution-filter
                        static
                        no bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**
- `allow-static`: Permits BGP to use static routes (excluding `0/0` default) for next-hop resolution.
- `resolution filter`: Restricts resolution to explicitly allowed tunnel types.
- `resolution-filter static`: Enables static routes in the filter.
- `no bgp`: Disables BGP tunnels to ensure only static routes are used.

This configuration ensures BGP uses only your custom static paths for labeled IPv4 traffic while ignoring the default route and other tunnel types.
