## User question:
Hey, I’m working with a Nokia 7750 SR in a mixed-vendor setup where some older gear chokes on BGP neighbors using AS numbers beyond 65535. What’s the best way to lock down the router so it only allows peers with the classic two-byte AS format and rejects anything larger?
---
## Proposed answer:
To lock down the router to only allow BGP peers with two-byte AS numbers (≤65535), configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    dynamic-neighbor-limit 0
```

This command disables dynamic BGP neighbor sessions, ensuring only statically configured neighbors (which must be manually set with valid two-byte AS numbers) are permitted.
