Replace `"CLUSTER_GROUP"` with your BGP group name and `<cluster-id>` with a unique cluster identifier (e.g., an IP address like `192.0.2.1`). This marks peers in the group as route reflector clients and activates loop prevention by appending the cluster ID to reflected routes.
