To bind the INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY filtering rule for controlling route advertisements to internal BGP neighbors, use the following CLI configuration commands. Replace `<neighbor-ip>` with the actual IP address of the BGP neighbor and ensure the policy is configured as an extended community policy.

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "INTERNAL"
        type internal
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            outbound-route-filtering
                extended-community
                    send-orf INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY
                    accept-orf
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `type internal`: Designates the BGP peer as internal.  
- `outbound-route-filtering`: Enables BGP outbound route filtering (ORF) for the neighbor.  
- `extended-community`: Opens configuration for extended community-based filtering.  
- `send-orf INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY`: Advertises the specified extended community policy (INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY) to the neighbor to control which prefixes are accepted.  
- `accept-orf`: Allows the router to receive and apply ORF filters from the neighbor.  

This configuration ensures only prefixes matching INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY are exchanged, preventing accidental route leaks.
