On a Nokia 7750 SR, when setting up BGP across multiple peer clusters, what’s the best way to tweak the reflection settings to make sure routes are shared efficiently between groups without creating bottlenecks or redundant chatter?
---
## Proposed answer:
```
configure router bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location 1 primary-ip-address <location1_loopback>
        location 2 primary-ip-address <location2_loopback>
        # Add more locations as needed
    exit
    group "CLUSTER1_PEERS"
        cluster <cluster1_id> orr-location 1 allow-local-fallback
    exit
    group "CLUSTER2_PEERS"
        cluster <cluster2_id> orr-location 2 allow-local-fallback
    exit
    # Additional cluster groups follow same pattern
exit
