- `prefix-limit ipv6 5000`: Sets a maximum limit of 5000 IPv6 routes.  
- `threshold 75`: Triggers a warning when 75% of the limit (3750 routes) is reached.  
- `log-only`: Ensures the session stays up if the limit is exceeded and logs both threshold/max-limit events.  

Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP. Log events (threshold/max triggers) are automatically generated and visible via system logs.
