Based on your request to limit BGP-labeled routes to specific LSP types like RSVP or SR, here are the required CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution filter
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp
                        sr-ospf
                        # Add other SR types as needed (e.g. sr-isis, sr-te)
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Key steps implemented:**
1. Set BGP labeled routes resolution mode to `filter` to enforce selective tunnel binding
2. Specified allowed tunnel types (`rsvp` and `sr-ospf`) under the resolution filter
3. Explicitly disabled all other tunnel types by omission

**To customize:**
- Replace `ipv4` with `ipv6` if working with IPv6 routes
- Add/remove specific tunnel types in the `resolution-filter` section (e.g. `sr-isis`, `sr-te`)
- Use `no <tunnel-type>` commands to explicitly block unwanted tunnel bindings

This configuration ensures BGP-labeled routes will only bind to RSVP and SR-OSPF LSPs in your path resolution policy.
