To adjust BGP next-hop handling for route installation on a Nokia 7750 SR, navigate to the specific hierarchy based on the route type:

### **For Labeled Routes (e.g., Labeled-IPv4, Labeled-IPv6, VPN):**
```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family [label-ipv4 | label-ipv6 | vpn]
                    resolution filter
                    resolution-filter [tunnel-type]
```

**Example:** Set labeled-IPv4 routes to resolve next-hops **only via RSVP tunnels**:
```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution filter
                    resolution-filter rsvp
```

### **For Unlabeled Routes (e.g., IPv4, IPv6):**
```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family [ipv4 | ipv6]
                resolution [any | filter | disabled]
```

**Example:** Disable next-hop resolution for unlabeled IPv6 routes:
```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv6
                resolution disabled
```

### **Key Parameters:**
- `resolution`:  
  - `any`: Use all supported tunnels (default).  
  - `filter`: Restrict to tunnels specified in `resolution-filter`.  
  - `disabled`: Disable next-hop resolution.  
- `resolution-filter`: Specify tunnel types (e.g., `ldp`, `rsvp`, `sr-te`). **Required** when `resolution filter` is set (labeled routes only).

> **Note:**  
> - `resolution-filter` is **only available under `labeled-routes`**.  
> - Replace `[tunnel-type]` with actual tunnel protocols (e.g., `ldp`, `rsvp`).  
> - Use `no resolution-filter [tunnel-type]` to remove a tunnel type from the filter.
