To ensure BGP peers maintain the session during your router's reboot and wait up to 10 minutes, configure the following:

```
/configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 600
```

### Explanation:
- **`graceful-restart`** enables BGP graceful restart capabilities at the global level.
- **`restart-time 600`** explicitly sets the advertised restart timer to 600 seconds (10 minutes), overriding the default. Peers honoring graceful restart will retain routes and await re-establishment within this window.

### Optional per-group/per-neighbor override:
If specific peers/groups require different timers, apply the configuration under the group or neighbor context:
```
/configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME"
    graceful-restart
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 600
```

### Key Notes:
1. Peers must support BGP graceful restart (RFC 4724) and operate in helper mode (default behavior on most devices).
2. Ensure the reboot completes within 600 seconds; otherwise, peers will timeout.
3. The `restart-time` is strictly an advisory value—peers decide locally whether to honor it.
